<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Ijesha Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1893 CE (approx.) · capital Ilesa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Yoruba kingdom of the eastern uplands centred on Ilesa, whose war leader Ogedengbe led the Ekiti Parapo against Ibadan.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Ijesha tradition holds that the kingdom was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajibogun">Ajibogun</a>, called Obokun, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oduduwa">Oduduwa</a> who fetched sea water to cure his father's blindness and was rewarded with a crown. His title, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owa-obokun">Owa Obokun</a>, became that of the kings of Ijesha, who later fixed their capital at Ilesa.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owa-obokun">Owa</a> ruled with a council of town chiefs and war chiefs over farming communities in a fertile hill country. Ijesha was a regional power among the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a>, trading kola and cloth. In the 19th century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibadan">Ibadan's</a> expansion brought defeat and occupation, and the Ijesha warlord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ogedengbe">Ogedengbe</a> rose to lead resistance.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Ijesha joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ekiti-parapo">Ekiti Parapo</a> alliance in the long Kiriji war against <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ibadan">Ibadan</a> from 1877, until a British-brokered treaty of 1886 halted the fighting and the war camps were dispersed in 1893. It then came under British control within <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/protectorate-of-southern-nigeria">Southern Nigeria</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owa-obokun">Owa Obokun</a> still reigns at Ilesa in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osun-state">Osun State</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 CE – 1893 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.55%;width:7.82%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1893 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ilesa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ajibogun</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Yoruba religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Yoruba</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/nigeria">Nigeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ijesha, Ilesa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1696&amp;focus=ijesha-kingdom" aria-label="Ijesha Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4811 1892 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ijesha Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5131 2148L5108 2158"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5108 2158h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5131 2148h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5131 2148h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ilesa. <a href="/atlas?year=1696&amp;focus=ijesha-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

